Conversations that need your attention, one row per person. Reply or mark done.

By default, only actionable topics appear: unanswered directed requests and due reminders you explicitly set. Recent, unread, pinned, archived and sent-only mail do not qualify just because they exist. Use `mxr messages list --turn all` for All conversations, including history in Recent and Quiet; `messages person EMAIL` also retains that person's history. Each row is a person, merged across their addresses; a group thread is its own row. The preview is what they asked, from the conversation's gist when one is cached, else their latest new text.

Usage: mxr messages [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  list    Conversations needing attention (the default), or an explicit history view
  person  One person's page: how you know them, every topic, and the selected topic as a conversation of what each message newly says [alias: show]
  ack     Got it: reply with a short acknowledgement in your usual greeting and sign-off for that person. --dry-run prints the exact text
  merge   Make several addresses one person, by hand. mxr only ever suggests a merge (same name, you've written to both); --suggestions lists them
  split   Take an address back out of the person it was merged into
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --account <ACCOUNT>
          Limit to one account; the default covers every account

      --format <FORMAT>
          [possible values: table, json, jsonl, csv, ids]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
